::notice file=fixtures/vulnerable-examples/missing-auth/src/lib.rs,line=33,col=10,endLine=33,endColumn=13,title=SG-007 missing-ttl-extension::This contract writes persistent storage but never extends its TTL; entries will be archived when their TTL expires%0AExtend the TTL where entries are written or read, e.g. `env.storage().persistent().extend_ttl(&key, THRESHOLD, EXTEND_TO)` and `env.storage().instance().extend_ttl(THRESHOLD, EXTEND_TO)` in frequently called functions.%0Ahttps://github.com/petermuazu/Soroban-Security-Rules-Toolkit/blob/main/docs/rules/SG-007.md
::warning file=fixtures/vulnerable-examples/missing-auth/src/lib.rs,line=62,col=16,endLine=62,endColumn=24,title=SG-001 missing-authorization::Exported function `withdraw` transfers tokens out of the contract without an authorization check%0AReview whether this operation requires `address.require_auth()` (on the affected user or the stored admin). If the function is intentionally permissionless, add `// stellar-guard-ignore SG-001 -- <reason>`.%0Ahttps://github.com/petermuazu/Soroban-Security-Rules-Toolkit/blob/main/docs/rules/SG-001.md
::warning file=fixtures/vulnerable-examples/missing-auth/src/lib.rs,line=67,col=34,endLine=67,endColumn=37,title=SG-001 missing-authorization::Exported function `set_admin` modifies privileged configuration without an authorization check%0AReview whether this operation requires `address.require_auth()` (on the affected user or the stored admin). If the function is intentionally permissionless, add `// stellar-guard-ignore SG-001 -- <reason>`.%0Ahttps://github.com/petermuazu/Soroban-Security-Rules-Toolkit/blob/main/docs/rules/SG-001.md
::notice file=fixtures/vulnerable-examples/missing-auth/src/lib.rs,line=67,col=34,endLine=67,endColumn=37,title=SG-007 missing-ttl-extension::This contract writes instance storage but never extends its TTL; entries will be archived when their TTL expires%0AExtend the TTL where entries are written or read, e.g. `env.storage().persistent().extend_ttl(&key, THRESHOLD, EXTEND_TO)` and `env.storage().instance().extend_ttl(THRESHOLD, EXTEND_TO)` in frequently called functions.%0Ahttps://github.com/petermuazu/Soroban-Security-Rules-Toolkit/blob/main/docs/rules/SG-007.md
::notice file=fixtures/vulnerable-examples/missing-auth/src/lib.rs,line=67,col=34,endLine=67,endColumn=37,title=SG-010 missing-admin-events::Exported function `set_admin` modifies privileged configuration without publishing a Soroban event%0APublish an event with `env.events().publish(..)` so off-chain consumers can monitor this change.%0Ahttps://github.com/petermuazu/Soroban-Security-Rules-Toolkit/blob/main/docs/rules/SG-010.md
::warning file=fixtures/vulnerable-examples/missing-auth/src/lib.rs,line=72,col=24,endLine=72,endColumn=52,title=SG-001 missing-authorization::Exported function `upgrade` upgrades the contract WASM without an authorization check%0AReview whether this operation requires `address.require_auth()` (on the affected user or the stored admin). If the function is intentionally permissionless, add `// stellar-guard-ignore SG-001 -- <reason>`.%0Ahttps://github.com/petermuazu/Soroban-Security-Rules-Toolkit/blob/main/docs/rules/SG-001.md
::notice file=fixtures/vulnerable-examples/missing-auth/src/lib.rs,line=72,col=24,endLine=72,endColumn=52,title=SG-010 missing-admin-events::Exported function `upgrade` upgrades the contract without publishing a Soroban event%0APublish an event with `env.events().publish(..)` so off-chain consumers can monitor this change.%0Ahttps://github.com/petermuazu/Soroban-Security-Rules-Toolkit/blob/main/docs/rules/SG-010.md
::warning file=fixtures/vulnerable-examples/missing-auth/src/lib.rs,line=77,col=9,endLine=77,endColumn=22,title=SG-001 missing-authorization::Exported function `credit` writes contract storage (via `write_balance`) without an authorization check%0AReview whether this operation requires `address.require_auth()` (on the affected user or the stored admin). If the function is intentionally permissionless, add `// stellar-guard-ignore SG-001 -- <reason>`.%0Ahttps://github.com/petermuazu/Soroban-Security-Rules-Toolkit/blob/main/docs/rules/SG-001.md
::warning file=fixtures/vulnerable-examples/missing-auth/src/lib.rs,line=77,col=9,endLine=77,endColumn=22,title=SG-006 negative-amount::`credit` stores or accounts `amount: i128` without rejecting negative values%0AAdd `if amount <= 0 { panic_with_error!(..) }` (or `< 0` if zero is allowed) before using it.%0Ahttps://github.com/petermuazu/Soroban-Security-Rules-Toolkit/blob/main/docs/rules/SG-006.md
::warning file=fixtures/vulnerable-examples/missing-auth/src/lib.rs,line=83,col=34,endLine=83,endColumn=37,title=SG-001 missing-authorization::Exported function `set_token` writes contract storage without an authorization check%0AReview whether this operation requires `address.require_auth()` (on the affected user or the stored admin). If the function is intentionally permissionless, add `// stellar-guard-ignore SG-001 -- <reason>`.%0Ahttps://github.com/petermuazu/Soroban-Security-Rules-Toolkit/blob/main/docs/rules/SG-001.md
::warning file=fixtures/vulnerable-examples/missing-auth/src/lib.rs,line=92,col=16,endLine=92,endColumn=24,title=SG-001 missing-authorization::Exported function `withdraw_to` transfers tokens out of the contract, but authorizes only on some code paths (inside a branch, loop or closure)%0AReview whether this operation requires `address.require_auth()` (on the affected user or the stored admin). If the function is intentionally permissionless, add `// stellar-guard-ignore SG-001 -- <reason>`.%0Ahttps://github.com/petermuazu/Soroban-Security-Rules-Toolkit/blob/main/docs/rules/SG-001.md
::warning file=fixtures/vulnerable-examples/missing-auth/src/lib.rs,line=102,col=9,endLine=102,endColumn=22,title=SG-001 missing-authorization::Exported function `move_balance` decreases a value keyed by `from`, but only `caller` authorizes%0ACall `from.require_auth()` before debiting it, or check an allowance granted by `from` to the caller.%0Ahttps://github.com/petermuazu/Soroban-Security-Rules-Toolkit/blob/main/docs/rules/SG-001.md
::warning file=fixtures/vulnerable-examples/missing-auth/src/lib.rs,line=102,col=9,endLine=102,endColumn=22,title=SG-006 negative-amount::`move_balance` stores or accounts `amount: i128` without rejecting negative values%0AAdd `if amount <= 0 { panic_with_error!(..) }` (or `< 0` if zero is allowed) before using it.%0Ahttps://github.com/petermuazu/Soroban-Security-Rules-Toolkit/blob/main/docs/rules/SG-006.md
::warning file=fixtures/vulnerable-examples/missing-auth/src/lib.rs,line=109,col=14,endLine=109,endColumn=35,title=SG-001 missing-authorization::Exported function `withdraw_signed` calls `require_auth_for_args` without `to`, `amount` in the signed arguments%0AInclude every amount and address that the call acts on in the `require_auth_for_args` arguments, or use `require_auth()` so the full invocation is signed.%0Ahttps://github.com/petermuazu/Soroban-Security-Rules-Toolkit/blob/main/docs/rules/SG-001.md
